-## What is this?
+## 🔥 What's New (v1.2 — March 2026)
 
-_y is a visual orchestration layer for AI agents. Most multi-agent frameworks run in a terminal — logs scroll, JSON outputs, you have no idea what's happening between agents.
+| Update | Description |
+|--------|-------------|
+| **🛠️ Agent Tool Binding** | All 30 agents now have real executable tools — 15 tools, zero API keys. Web search, market data, security headers, GitHub issues, and more. |
+| **🧠 Dynamic Memory** | Agents recall past interactions. Top 10 memories (by importance) injected into every conversation for contextual, personalized responses. |
+| **📊 Hierarchical Execution** | Directives flow through the org chart: Staff → Manager → Director → C-Suite. Each tier builds on prior analysis with independent verification. |
+| **🏛️ LLM-by-Rank** | Stronger models for higher ranks. C-Suite = Claude Opus, Director = Claude Sonnet + Qwen3, Manager = Gemini Flash + Gemma3, Staff = MiniMax + Gemini. Byzantine principle preserved. |
+| **🗺️ 30-Agent Org Chart** | Workflow graph now shows all 30 agents in tier-based hierarchy. Click any agent for full details. |
+| **🔄 M4 Worker Support** | Chat worker runs on dedicated hardware (128GB Mac Studio) for local Ollama models + Claude CLI + Gemini API. |
 
-_y makes agent work **visible**. See who's analyzing what, how reports flow between functions, where agents disagree, and which LLM provider catches what the others miss. Configure agents for your business functions — marketing, engineering, risk, finance — and watch them work independently before a synthesis agent combines everything.
+![Demo](./docs/demo.gif)
 
-Run locally with **Ollama** (free), or use cloud LLMs (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google). Mix different providers per function for broader coverage.
+<details>
