+## Architecture
+
+```mermaid
+graph TB
+    subgraph "Frontend Layer"
+        UI[Next.js App Router]
+        Components[React Components]
+        Flow[ReactFlow Visualization]
+    end
+    
+    subgraph "Business Logic"
+        Engine[Simulation Engine]
+        Memory[Agent Memory]
+        Planner[Decision Planner]
+    end
+    
+    subgraph "AI Layer"
+        Claude[Claude Opus/Sonnet]
+        Gemini[Gemini Flash/Pro]
+        Ollama[Local Models]
+    end
+    
+    subgraph "Data Layer"
+        Supabase[Supabase PostgreSQL]
+        Config[Agent Configuration]
+    end
+    
+    UI --> Engine
+    Components --> Flow
+    Engine --> Memory
+    Engine --> Planner
+    Memory --> Supabase
+    Planner --> Claude
+    Planner --> Gemini
+    Planner --> Ollama
+    Config --> Engine
 ```
 
-## The Philosophy
+### Project Structure
 
-> **"No Consensus, Just Counsel"**
+```
+src/
+├── app/           # Next.js App Router pages & API routes
+├── components/    # React components
+│   ├── TowerView.tsx        # Main tower visualization
+│   ├── CompanySettings.tsx  # Company connection & profile
+│   ├── MeetingRoom.tsx      # War Room (meetings + simulations)
+│   ├── ChairmanDashboard.tsx # CEO dashboard
+│   ├── AgentFlowGraph.tsx   # Agent workflow visualization
+│   └── ...
+├── data/          # Agent configs, floor data, i18n
+├── engine/        # Simulation engine, memory, planner
+├── lib/           # Utilities, Supabase client, connectors
+├── context/       # React contexts (Language, Report)
+└── hooks/         # Custom React hooks
+```
+
+## The 30 Agents
 
-Most multi-agent frameworks let AI agents vote and reach consensus. We don\'t. Based on research into the [Byzantine Generals Problem in LLM agents](https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.04838), democratic consensus among AI agents is structurally unreliable.
+Our AI workforce is organized across 10 floors with clear hierarchies and specialized roles:
+
+| # | Agent | Role | Floor | Department | LLM |
+|---|-------|------|-------|------------|-----|
+| 30 | Counsely | Chief of Staff | 10F | Chairman's Office | Claude Opus |
+| 01 | Tasky | Task Management | 9F | Planning & Coordination | Claude Opus |
+| 02 | Finy | Financial Planning | 9F | Planning & Coordination | Claude Sonnet |
+| 03 | Legaly | Legal Affairs | 9F | Planning & Coordination | Qwen3 32B |
+| 04 | Skepty | Risk Analysis | 8F | Risk Challenge | Qwen3 32B |
+| 05 | Audity | Auditing | 8F | Audit | Claude Sonnet |
+| 06 | Pixely | UI/UX Design | 7F | Software Development | Gemma3 27B |
+| 07 | Buildy | Full-stack Development | 7F | Software Development | MiniMax M2.5 |
+| 08 | Testy | QA/Testing | 7F | Software Development | MiniMax M2.5 |
+| 09 | Buzzy | Social Media | 6F | Content Division | Claude Sonnet |
+| 10 | Wordy | Copywriting | 6F | Content Division | Claude Sonnet |
+| 11 | Edity | Video Editing | 6F | Content Division | Gemma3 27B |
+| 12 | Searchy | SEO/Research | 6F | Content Division | Gemini Flash |
+| 13 | Growthy | Growth Hacking | 5F | Marketing Division | Gemma3 27B |
+| 14 | Logoy | Brand Design | 5F | Marketing Division | Gemma3 27B |
+| 15 | Helpy | Customer Support | 5F | Marketing Division | Gemini Flash |
+| 16 | Clicky | Ad Management | 5F | Marketing Division | Gemini Flash |
+| 17 | Selly | Sales Strategy | 5F | Marketing Division | Gemini Flash |
+| 18 | Stacky | Infrastructure | 4F | ICT Division | MiniMax M2.5 |
+| 19 | Watchy | Monitoring | 4F | ICT Division | MiniMax M2.5 |
+| 20 | Guardy | Security | 4F | ICT Division | Qwen3 32B |
+| 21 | Hiry | Operations Support | 3F | Human Resources | Claude Sonnet |
+| 22 | Evaly | Data Analytics | 3F | Human Resources | Claude Sonnet |
+| 23 | Quanty | Quantitative Analysis | 2F | _y Capital | Qwen3 32B |
+| 24 | Tradey | Trading | 2F | _y Capital | Qwen3 32B |
+| 25 | Globy | Global Markets | 2F | _y Capital | Gemini Flash |
+| 26 | Fieldy | Field Research | 2F | _y Capital | Gemini Flash |
+| 27 | Hedgy | Hedge Strategy | 2F | _y Capital | Qwen3 32B |
+| 28 | Valuey | Valuation | 2F | _y Capital | Qwen3 32B |
+| 29 | Opsy | Operations | 1F | _y SaaS | MiniMax M2.5 |
+
+### LLM Distribution Strategy
+
+LLMs are assigned **by hierarchy** — stronger models for higher ranks, different architectures within the same tier for Byzantine resilience:
+
+| Tier | Model(s) | Agents | Purpose |
+|------|----------|--------|---------|
+| **C-Suite** (3) | Claude Opus | Counsely, Tasky, Finy | Strategic synthesis, final judgment |
+| **Director** (9) | Claude Sonnet + Qwen3 32B | Legaly, Audity, Buildy, Buzzy, Growthy, Quanty (Sonnet) · Skepty, Stacky, Opsy (Qwen3) | Deep analysis + cross-architecture verification |
+| **Manager** (13) | Gemini Flash + Gemma3 27B | Searchy, Testy, Edity, Watchy, Hiry, Tradey, Hedgy (Flash) · Pixely, Wordy, Guardy, Evaly, Globy, Valuey (Gemma3) | Fast execution + alternative perspective |
+| **Staff** (5) | MiniMax M2.5 + Gemini Flash | Logoy, Clicky, Fieldy (MiniMax) · Helpy, Selly (Flash) | Lightweight data collection |
+
+**Key principle**: Same-tier agents use **different LLM architectures** so no two agents analyzing the same issue share the same model biases.
+
+## Configuration
+
+### Company Settings (`company.yml`)
+
+Define your AI company in a single YAML file:
+
+```yaml
+company:
+  name: "Acme Corp"
+  industry: "saas"
+  description: "AI-powered analytics platform"
+  team_size: 15
+
+floors:
+  - level: 10
+    name: "Executive"
+    agents: [counsely, tasky]
+  - level: 9
+    name: "Strategy"
+    agents: [finy, legaly]
+  # ... add up to 10 floors
+
+agents:
+  - id: custom_agent
+    name: "DataBot"
+    tier: "Manager"
+    floor: 4
+    department: "Data Engineering"
+    llm: "gemini-flash"
+    role: "analyst"
+    desc: "Data pipeline monitoring and optimization"
+```
 
-Instead: Each agent analyzes independently → They discuss in meetings → Counsely synthesizes → **You decide.** The human stays in the loop.
+Company profile settings are in `src/data/company-config.ts`:
+- Company name, description, products
+- Target customers and values
+- Agent response rules
 
-30 agents, zero consensus — by design.
