-## Corporate Hierarchy
+### LLM Configuration
 
-Unlike flat agent frameworks, _y agents have ranks and reporting lines — just like a real company:
+Swap any agent's LLM in `agent-config.ts`:
 
-```
-Chairman (You)
-├── Counsely — Chief of Staff (synthesis, final briefing)
-├── Tasky — Planning Director
-│   ├── Finy (Finance) · Legaly (Legal)
-│   ├── Buzzy → Wordy, Edity, Searchy (Content)
-│   ├── Growthy → Logoy, Helpy, Clicky, Selly (Marketing)
-│   ├── Stacky → Watchy, Guardy (ICT)
-│   ├── Hiry → Evaly (HR)
-│   ├── Buildy → Pixely, Testy (Engineering)
-│   └── Opsy (Operations)
-├── Skepty — Risk Director (independent challenge)
-├── Audity — Audit (independent review)
-└── Quanty — Capital Director
-    └── Tradey, Globy, Fieldy, Hedgy, Valuey
+```typescript
+const LLM_MODELS = {
+  // Cloud APIs (fast, paid)
+  claude_opus:    { type: 'anthropic', model: 'claude-opus-4-20250514' },
+  claude_sonnet:  { type: 'anthropic', model: 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514' },
+  gemini_flash:   { type: 'gemini',    model: 'gemini-2.5-flash' },
+
+  // Local via Ollama (free, slower)
+  qwen3_32b:      { type: 'ollama', model: 'qwen3:32b' },
+  gemma3_27b:     { type: 'ollama', model: 'gemma3:27b' },
+
+  // Add your own
+  gpt4o_mini:     { type: 'openai', model: 'gpt-4o-mini' },
+  llama3:         { type: 'ollama', model: 'llama3.3:70b' },
+};
 ```
 
-**Key design:** Risk (Skepty) and Audit (Audity) report directly to the Chairman — never to the departments they review. Just like a real corporate governance structure.
+**Byzantine Principle**: Agents analyzing the same issue (analysis ↔ check ↔ synthesis) must use different LLM architectures to avoid correlated failures.
 
-## The 30 Agents
+| Role | Recommended | Why |
+|------|------------|-----|
+| Research/Search | Gemini Flash | Fast, good at retrieval |
+| Analysis/Finance | Claude Sonnet | Strong reasoning |
+| Synthesis/Strategy | Claude Opus | Best judgment |
+| Risk/Audit | Different from analyst | Byzantine independence |
+| Dev/Ops | Ollama local or MiniMax | Cost-effective |
+
+### API Extension
 
-| Floor | Department | Agents | Default LLM |
-|-------|-----------|--------|-------------|
-| 10F | Chairman\'s Office | Counsely (Chief of Staff) | Largest available |
-| 9F | Planning | Tasky, Finy, Legaly | Strategy model |
-| 8F | Risk & Audit | Skepty, Audity | Analysis model |
-| 7F | Engineering | Pixely, Buildy, Testy | Dev model |
-| 6F | Content | Buzzy, Wordy, Edity, Searchy | Research model |
-| 5F | Marketing | Growthy, Logoy, Helpy, Clicky, Selly | Research model |
-| 4F | ICT | Stacky, Watchy, Guardy | Dev model |
-| 3F | HR | Hiry, Evaly | Analysis model |
-| 2F | Capital | Quanty, Tradey, Globy, Fieldy, Hedgy, Valuey | Analysis model |
-| 1F | Operations | Opsy | Dev model |
+The directive pipeline is the core execution engine:
 
-**Byzantine Principle**: Agents on the same issue with analysis ↔ check ↔ synthesis roles use different LLM architectures to avoid correlated failures.
+```
+POST /api/directives        → Create directive (title + description)
+POST /api/directive/assign  → Counsely assigns agents (Claude Opus)
+POST /api/directive/execute → Create chat_queue tasks per agent
+POST /api/directive/complete → Collect responses → generate report
+```
 
-## Adding Custom Agents
+**Adding a new API endpoint:**
 
 ```typescript
-// src/data/agent-config.ts
-{
-  id: \'datay\',
-  number: \'31\',
-  name: \'Datay\',
-  tier: \'Manager\',
-  floor: 4,
-  department: \'ICT Division\',
-  reportTo: \'stacky\',
-  llm: LLM_MODELS.qwen3_32b,
-  role: \'analyst\',
-  desc: \'Data Engineering\',
-  emoji: \'\'
+// src/app/api/custom/route.ts
+import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from 'next/server';
+
+export async function POST(req: NextRequest) {
+  const { agentId, task } = await req.json();
+
+  // Insert into chat_queue — M4 worker picks it up automatically
+  const res = await fetch(`${SUPABASE_URL}/rest/v1/chat_queue`, {
+    method: 'POST',
+    headers: {
+      'apikey': SUPABASE_KEY,
+      'Authorization': `Bearer ${SUPABASE_KEY}`,
+      'Content-Type': 'application/json',
+    },
+    body: JSON.stringify({
+      agent_id: agentId,
+      message: task,
+      status: 'pending',
+    }),
+  });
+
+  return NextResponse.json({ ok: true });
 }
-
-// Add photo: public/agents/datay.png
-// Add persona: src/data/personas.ts
 ```
 
-## Directive Pipeline
+The chat worker (`scripts/chat-worker.ts`) polls `chat_queue` and routes to the correct LLM based on the agent's config. No code changes needed — just insert a row.
 
-The core execution engine:
+## Development
 
-1. **Chairman issues directive** (Dashboard)
-2. **Counsely assigns agents** (Ollama AI selection)
-3. **Agents execute** (chat_queue → worker → Ollama)
-4. **Report generated** (auto-compiled from all responses)
+### Available Scripts
+
+```bash
+npm run dev          # Start development server
+npm run build        # Build for production
+npm run start        # Start production server
+npm run lint         # Run ESLint
+npx tsx scripts/chat-worker.ts  # Start chat worker (on your GPU machine)
+```
+
+### Project Structure
 
 ```
-POST /api/directives        → Create directive
-POST /api/directive/assign   → AI agent assignment
-POST /api/directive/execute  → Queue agent tasks
-POST /api/directive/complete → Compile report
-GET  /api/directive/status   → Poll progress
+src/
+├── app/api/          # API routes (directives, chat, decisions)
+├── components/       # React components (TowerView, Dashboard, GlassPanel)
+├── data/             # Agent config, floor config, company config, personas
+├── context/          # React contexts (Lang, Report)
+├── lib/              # Utilities (markdown, floor-icons)
+scripts/
+├── chat-worker.ts    # LLM queue worker (runs on M4/GPU server)
+├── searchy-news.ts   # Automated news collection
+sql/
+├── schema.sql        # Full database schema (9 tables)
+public/agents/        # Agent avatar images (30 PNGs)
 ```
 
-## Tech Stack
+## Deployment
 
-- **Frontend**: Next.js 16, React 19, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui
-- **Database**: SQLite (better-sqlite3) — zero config
-- **AI**: Ollama (local) / OpenAI / Anthropic / Google — your choice
-- **Icons**: Lucide React
+The easiest way to deploy is using Vercel:
 
-## Prerequisites
+[![Deploy with Vercel](https://vercel.com/button)](https://vercel.com/new/clone?repository-url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fantryu2b%2Fy-company)
 
-- Node.js 18+
-- **Option A (Local):** [Ollama](https://ollama.ai) installed + 8GB+ RAM
-- **Option B (Cloud):** API key from OpenAI, Anthropic, or Google
+1. Connect your GitHub repository to Vercel
+2. Set environment variables in Vercel dashboard
+3. Deploy automatically on every push to main
 
